  "result": "I fixed `IntRange` with `clamp=True` returning a value outside the range when a bound is open (`min_open` or `max_open`). `tests/test_types.py` now passes (43 passed, 2 skipped); I didn't run the full suite.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` moved the wrong way from an open bound. It computed `bound - dir`, so `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1` instead of `1`. Likewise, `max=5, max_open=True` turned `9` into `6` instead of `4`. It now uses `bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** I added two clamp cases with open bounds to the existing parametrized test in `tests/test_types.py`.\n\n**Changelog:** I added an \"Unreleased\" entry to `CHANGES.md`, as CLAUDE.md asks. There was no unreleased section, so I created one at the top. Git also warned that it will convert that file's line endings to CRLF the next time it touches it.\n\nI made no docs changes, since this is a bug fix and no documented behaviour changed.",
